<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sikhism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sikh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sikhism is a monotheistic religion founded by Guru Nanak in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> in the late fifteenth and early sixteenth centuries. Its later Gurus created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalsa">Khalsa</a>, a community of initiated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhs">Sikhs</a>, in response to persecution. Sikhism was the defining identity of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amritsar">Amritsar</a> as its spiritual centre, and accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a> also refer to the Sikhs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sikhism.jpg" alt="Sikhism" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oleg Yunakov · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hamandir_Sahib_(Golden_Temple).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
